        "facts": ["Hegel saw the play as family and divine law against state and human law.", "On this reading each side destroys itself by refusing the other's claim.", "Critics answer that the gods' verdict in the play favors Antigone.", "A defensible position says what would count as one side being simply right."],
        "misconceptions": ["Saying both sides have a point means neither did anything wrong.", "A play can only have one correct moral."] },
