        "concept": "american-dream", "definition": "The belief that anyone can rise through effort to prosperity and a life of their choosing.",
        "facts": ["Gatsby rises from poverty but East Egg old money never accepts him.", "The green light represents what Gatsby reaches for.", "Myrtle and George Wilson are crushed by their pursuit and their poverty.", "A strong answer distinguishes the dream itself from its corruption."],
