        "facts": ["Lear asks his daughters to state their love publicly for a share of land.", "Goneril and Regan flatter him.", "Cordelia says she loves him according to her bond.", "Kent is banished for defending her.", "A strong answer considers whether she could have been honest more gently."],
        "misconceptions": ["Cordelia simply does not love her father enough.", "Honesty is always costless and obviously right."] },
      { "key": "lear-responsibility", "title": "Assess Lear's responsibility for his suffering", "description": "Weighs how far Lear causes his own fate and how far he is wronged.",
