        "facts": ["Lear wants a king's honors without a king's power.", "He disowns Cordelia and banishes Kent.", "Goneril and Regan strip his retinue and shut him out.", "He says he is a man more sinned against than sinning."],
        "misconceptions": ["Lear deserves everything that happens to him.", "Lear is entirely an innocent victim."] },
      { "key": "cosmic-justice", "title": "Decide whether the play shows any justice", "description": "Argues whether the play's world is governed by justice, chance or indifferent gods.",
        "concept": "cosmic-justice", "definition": "The question of whether the universe rewards good and punishes evil.",
