        "facts": ["Golding said society's defects come from human nature's defects.", "The boys bring British school habits and wartime attitudes with them.", "Not every boy becomes violent: Ralph, Piggy and Simon resist.", "Critics cite real cases of stranded children who cooperated.", "A strong answer says what evidence would test the claim."],
        "misconceptions": ["The novel proves that all humans are evil at heart.", "Fiction cannot tell us anything about real human nature."] },
      { "key": "ralph-jack", "title": "Compare Ralph's and Jack's leadership", "description": "Evaluates why Jack's leadership wins the boys' loyalty and what that says about authority.",
