      "Readers have seen the whale as God, nature, evil, the unknowable, or a blank on which people project meaning. Ahab has been read as a tragic hero of defiance, a tyrant who leads others to death, and a figure for American ambition. Critics also ask what to make of the ship's diverse crew and of Ishmael, who survives by drifting rather than by willing."
