      "Atticus is appointed to defend Tom Robinson, a Black man falsely accused of raping a white woman, Mayella Ewell. Atticus tells Scout that you never really understand a person until you consider things from his point of view. He tells the children it is a sin to kill a mockingbird, because mockingbirds do nothing but make music.",
      "At the trial Atticus shows that Mayella was beaten by someone who led with his left hand, as her father Bob Ewell does, while Tom's left arm was crippled in an accident. Tom testifies that he helped Mayella with chores and that he felt sorry for her. The all-white jury convicts him anyway. Tom is later shot while trying to escape from prison.",
